23
00:01:47,990 --> 00:01:51,910
if people don't know that your code is going to solve their problems then it might as well not even exist.

24
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:55,350
because they're not going to be able to find it they're not going to be able to use it.

25
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:01,350
and so as a software engineer i've seen how a lot of my friends sort of turn up their nose.

26
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:06,230
to the business marketing sides of the profession and say no i'm just a pure coder.

27
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:08,389
my job is to create engineering artifacts.

28
00:02:08,389 --> 00:02:12,470
and that's absolutely the most important part of the job.

29
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:17,350
and the thing that we do uniquely well as software engineers is creating technical artifacts.

30
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:19,670
but if we make these things and then we don't show them.

31
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:22,949
then they're not going to be able to help people.

32
00:02:22,949 --> 00:02:26,710
so writing is one of the best ways to share our work.

33
00:02:26,710 --> 00:02:29,510
and make sure that it has the impact that we're looking for.

34
